    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Thanks. In my current case, the interruption is due to a series of unexpected supply chain failures and local administrative delays that weren't explicitly listed in the clause. Does the \"beyond reasonable control\" standard usually cover these types of indirect disruptions, or is the scope typically restricted to more catastrophic, direct events?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
